       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 4250 mg three times daily comes to 12,750 mg/day, which is about five times the usual maximum for metformin. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day, or 3,000 mg/day in some references. A single 4,250 mg dose is also far above the usual 500\u20131,000 mg per dose. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis is serious, even with normal renal function.\n\nThis may be a typo. Did you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the usual max)\n- **425 mg**, which isn't a standard strength\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg** per dose, with a different frequency\n\nTell me the dose you intend and I'll enter it right away. If 4,250 mg really is what you want, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
